---
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import figmaV1 from "../assets/campaign-builder/graphics/campaign-figma-v1.png";
import sourceTemplate from "../assets/campaign-builder/graphics/campaign-3-files-template.png";

const documentedCapabilities = [
  "Tall, wide, and skinny source images",
  "Shared campaign copy",
  "Variations",
  "Frame-level overrides",
  "Template controls",
  "Live previews",
  "Selected export",
  "Reusable defaults and custom templates",
];
---

<div class="campaign-deep-content">
  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>01</span><div><p>Origin and business context</p><h3>The visible problem was a large Figma file. The broader problem was the workflow around it.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Repeated production</h4><p>Multi-channel campaigns required separate homepage, email, paid media, remarketing, merchandising, and tile assets. Changes had to be repeated across many artboards and formats.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Repeated coordination</h4><p>Approval required additional mockups and presentation work. Downstream teams still needed help finding assets, identifying the correct versions, and receiving organized handoffs.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>02</span><div><p>Figma V1</p><h3>The first system improved consistency without fully changing the workflow.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>A meaningful first step</h4><p>Figma V1 used components, variables, reusable layouts, and clickable presentation behavior. It brought more consistency to the work and made the campaign easier to present.</p></div>
      <div><h4>The remaining limit</h4><p>The system remained designer-only and fragile. It standardized the artboards, but campaign creation, presentation, and downstream delivery were still not one connected workflow.</p></div>
    </div>
    <MediaFrame label="Figma V1 campaign system">
      <img src={figmaV1.src} width={figmaV1.width} height={figmaV1.height} alt="Figma V1 showing reusable web and email campaign layouts alongside an export-oriented layer structure." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>03</span><div><p>System model</p><h3>Campaign content changes. Production rules should not need to be rebuilt each time.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="rule-comparison">
      <div><span>Campaign-specific</span><ul><li>Copy</li><li>Imagery</li><li>Logos</li><li>Variations</li></ul></div>
      <div><span>Reusable system rules</span><ul><li>Dimensions</li><li>Typography</li><li>Spacing</li><li>Positioning</li><li>Brand behavior</li><li>Templates</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <p class="chapter-intro">The source-image model uses tall, wide, and skinny inputs to support different output shapes without preparing each destination asset independently.</p>
    <MediaFrame label="Tall, wide, and skinny source-image setup">
      <img src={sourceTemplate.src} width={sourceTemplate.width} height={sourceTemplate.height} alt="Figma source-image setup showing tall, wide, and skinny image formats with crop guides and examples." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>04</span><div><p>Current workspace and controls</p><h3>The workspace keeps shared campaign decisions connected to every selected output.</h3></div></header>
    <p class="chapter-intro">The current product combines shared inputs, variations, template controls, previews, and export selection in one workspace. The goal is coordinated control, while preserving the ability to adjust an individual frame when needed.</p>
    <ul class="capability-list">{documentedCapabilities.map((capability) => <li>{capability}</li>)}</ul>
    <div class="decision-note"><strong>Create faster → Approve faster → Deliver cleaner</strong><p>The product connects the work that was previously split between artboard maintenance, presentation preparation, and manual file organization.</p></div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>05</span><div><p>Presentation and handoff</p><h3>One campaign remains connected through review and delivery.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="two-column-copy">
      <div><h4>Approval</h4><p>A one-click presentation workflow brings the selected campaign formats and variations into a coordinated review experience without creating another set of approval mockups.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Delivery</h4><p>One campaign produces one export, automatically named and organized into folders by channel and use. This gives downstream teams a clearer handoff and reduces the need to identify the correct versions manually.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>06</span><div><p>Current use and impact</p><h3>The tool supports concept direction as well as final asset delivery.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="usage-grid">
      <div><strong>~75%</strong><span>estimated production-time reduction</span></div>
      <div><strong>~10 min</strong><span>approximate final variation setup once source imagery is ready</span></div>
      <div><strong>Under 30 min</strong><span>for concept exploration</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="estimate">These figures are working workflow estimates, not a formal time study. Concept exploration timing is separate from final variation setup.</p>
    <div class="two-column-copy adoption-copy">
      <div><h4>How it is being used</h4><p>The tool has been used mainly to demo concepts and help visualize design direction. It has also been used to deliver final assets.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Rollout</h4><p>OGIO and CGPO designers are using the tool, with Callaway beginning adoption. The status remains live with active rollout and testing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>07</span><div><p>Future direction</p><h3>Broader self-service and Contentstack integration remain future work.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="future-panel">
      <div><span>In progress / exploring</span><h4>Controlled self-service</h4><p>Expand who can use the system while preserving the template rules and controls that keep the campaign coordinated.</p></div>
      <div><span>In progress</span><h4>Contentstack API</h4><p>Explore connecting campaign outputs to the content workflow through the Contentstack API. This is not a completed capability.</p></div>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  .campaign-deep-content { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .deep-chapter { padding-block: var(--space-8); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .deep-chapter > header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
  .deep-chapter > header > span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; }
  .deep-chapter > header p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .deep-chapter > header h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .two-column-copy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-7); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .two-column-copy h4 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .two-column-copy p, .chapter-intro { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .chapter-intro { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .deep-chapter :global(.media-frame) { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .rule-comparison, .future-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .rule-comparison > div, .future-panel > div { padding: var(--space-5); }
  .rule-comparison > div + div, .future-panel > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 4%, transparent); }
  .rule-comparison span, .future-panel span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .rule-comparison ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .rule-comparison li { padding-block: var(--space-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .rule-comparison li::before { margin-right: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); content: "—"; }
  .capability-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); list-style: none; }
  .capability-list li { padding: var(--space-3); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .capability-list li:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .capability-list li::before { margin-right: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); content: "—"; }
  .decision-note { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(13rem, 0.42fr) minmax(0, 0.58fr); gap: var(--space-5); margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-5); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-canvas); }
  .decision-note p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .usage-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .usage-grid > div { display: flex; min-height: 10rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .usage-grid > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .usage-grid strong { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-3); line-height: 1; }
  .usage-grid span { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .estimate { margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-5); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .adoption-copy { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .future-panel h4 { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .future-panel p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .two-column-copy, .rule-comparison, .future-panel, .decision-note { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rule-comparison > div + div, .future-panel > div + div { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 0; }
    .usage-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .usage-grid > div { min-height: 7rem; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .usage-grid > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .deep-chapter > header { grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; }
    .capability-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .capability-list li { border-right: 0; }
  }
</style>
